# ChatGPT schedulers — MAX LIMIT

When editing ChatGPT scheduled-task prompts in this repo:

## Edit parent `prompts/chatgpt/<task>.md` for

- Queue size, refill order, skip/never-SKIP rules, modes (FULL/CHAT-DELIVERY)
- Duplicate scan, filename collision, schema, delivery templates, privacy
- Bump the task prompt's `version:` header

Push to GitHub — the next scheduled run fetches via Pages (`?t=`). **No ChatGPT re-paste.**

## Do NOT edit `schedulers/*.scheduler.md` for behavior

Schedulers are **frozen one-time bootstrap**: connector + ordered fetch URL list only.

**FORBIDDEN:**
- Adding behavior rules to scheduler COPY blocks
- Bumping `baseline-version` for behavior/queue/skip changes
- Telling the user to re-paste the ChatGPT scheduled task after behavior-only changes

**Allowed scheduler edits:** Pages URL path, repo/branch, or mandatory fetch URL list changes → re-paste once.

Authoritative policy: `prompts/chatgpt/schedulers/README.md` § MAX LIMIT.

Also read: `prompts/chatgpt/SHARED.md` (fetched every run by ChatGPT tasks).
